      "title": "HR Information Systems (HRIS) Architecture: Workday, BambooHR, ADP & API Integrations",
      "summary": "Architect modern HR technology ecosystems: HRIS selection, system integration (ATS, Payroll, LMS), employee self-service (ESS), role-based permissions, and SOC 2 data privacy.",
      "readingTimeMinutes": 40,
      "videoUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F3_6eO8bQ2w",
      "body": "<h2>1. The HR Technology Ecosystem</h2>\n<p>Modern People Operations relies on an integrated tech stack to manage thousands of data transactions daily. The <strong>Human Resources Information System (HRIS)</strong>—also termed Human Capital Management (HCM) or Human Resource Management System (HRMS)—serves as the centralized, immutable 'Single Source of Truth' for all employee demographic, compensation, organizational, and lifecycle data.</p>\n<p>The HR Generalist must possess technical systems fluency: understanding database schemas, automated workflow routing, role-based security access, and API integration protocols.</p>\n<h2>2. HRIS Tiering & Vendor Landscape</h2>\n<table class=\"comparison-table\">\n  <thead><tr><th>Tier / Category</th><th>Representative Platforms</th><th>Target Market Size</th><th>Architectural Strengths</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><strong>Enterprise Global HCM</strong></td><td>Workday, SAP SuccessFactors, Oracle Cloud HCM</td><td>Large multinational enterprises (3,000+ to 500,000+ employees)</td><td>Infinite configurability, global tax engine, multi-currency ledger, complex matrixed org structures.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Mid-Market All-in-One</strong></td><td>Rippling, Gusto, BambooHR, Paylocity, UKG</td><td>Growth-stage companies (25 to 1,500 employees)</td><td>Rapid turnkey deployment, unified payroll/benefits/IT device management, user-friendly modern UI.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Legacy Enterprise Payroll</strong></td><td>ADP Workforce Now, Ceridian Dayforce</td><td>Mid-to-large corporate organizations</td><td>Heavy payroll tax compliance, statutory garnishment handling, time/attendance hardware integration.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>3. Core System Integrations & Data Flow Architecture</h2>\n<pre><code>[Applicant Tracking System (Greenhouse/Lever)]\n      |  (Candidate Hired Webhook -> JSON Payload)\n      v\n[Core HRIS (Workday / Rippling)]  <--- Master System of Record\n      |-- (Bi-Directional Sync) --> [Global Payroll Engine (ADP / Deel)]\n      |-- (SCIM Provisioning)   --> [Identity Provider (Okta / Azure AD)]\n      |-- (User Telemetry)      --> [Learning Management System (Nalanda LMS)]\n      |-- (API Event Stream)    --> [Benefits Administration Carrier Feeds (EDI 834)]</code></pre>\n<h2>4. Electronic Data Interchange (EDI) 834 Carrier Feeds</h2>\n<p>Benefits enrollment data is communicated between HRIS engines and medical/dental insurance carriers (Aetna, BlueCross, UnitedHealthcare) via standardized <strong>EDI 834</strong> files. BAs and HR Generalists audit EDI error reports weekly to ensure new hire enrollments, life-event changes, and terminations transmit cleanly without dropped coverage.</p>\n<h2>5. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & PII Data Privacy</h2>\n<p>HRIS platforms house the most sensitive data in an enterprise: Social Security numbers, bank routing codes, home addresses, compensation history, and medical leave records. Strict RBAC matrices ensure managers can view only job titles and direct report reviews, while blocking access to sensitive medical or compensation data.</p>"
