      "courseId": "CRS-HRO-001",
      "chapterNumber": 23,
      "title": "People Analytics & HR Dashboards: Turnover, eNPS, Cost-Per-Hire & Attrition Prediction",
      "summary": "Transform HR into a data-driven intelligence center: calculating voluntary vs. involuntary turnover, retention curves, employee lifetime value, and predictive attrition modeling.",
      "readingTimeMinutes": 41,
      "videoUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F3_6eO8bQ2w",
      "body": "<h2>1. The Shift to Evidence-Based People Analytics</h2>\n<p>For decades, human resources operated primarily on intuition, anecdotal feedback, and subjective impressions. In modern data-driven enterprises, People Analytics transforms workforce telemetry into actionable commercial intelligence. By applying rigorous quantitative models to employee data, HR Generalists predict attrition bottlenecks, optimize hiring velocity, evaluate manager effectiveness, and quantify the direct financial return on talent investments.</p>\n<h2>2. Core People Metrics and Standard Formulas</h2>\n<table class=\"comparison-table\">\n  <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Mathematical Formula</th><th>Strategic Purpose & Benchmark</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><strong>Annualized Turnover Rate</strong></td><td><code>(Total Terminations / Average Headcount) * 100</code></td><td>Overall organizational retention health (Healthy target: 10% to 15% annual turnover).</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Voluntary vs. Involuntary Turnover</strong></td><td><code>(Voluntary Resignations / Total Terminations) * 100</code></td><td>Distinguishes talent flight risk from performance management pruning.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>90-Day Early Attrition Rate</strong></td><td><code>(Terminations within 90 Days / Total Hires) * 100</code></td><td>Direct barometer of recruitment candidate quality and onboarding effectiveness. Target: &lt; 5%.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Employee Net Promoter Score (eNPS)</strong></td><td><code>% Promoters (Score 9-10) - % Detractors (Score 0-6)</code></td><td>Workforce engagement index (Range: -100 to +100; > +30 is strong, > +50 is world-class).</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><strong>Time-to-Productivity (TTP)</strong></td><td>Days from start date to achieving 100% standard operational quota/output.</td><td>Evaluates learning velocity and onboarding ramp efficiency.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>3. Retention Curves & Cohort Analysis</h2>\n<p>Mirroring customer retention modeling in product analytics, HR plots employee survival curves: tracking what percentage of a specific cohort (e.g., Q1 2024 engineering hires) remains employed after 30, 90, 180, 365, and 730 days. Cliff drops at month 12 frequently indicate equity cliff vesting turnover or broken promotional promises.</p>\n<h2>4. Predictive Attrition Modeling (Flight Risk Scoring)</h2>\n<p>Advanced People Ops teams deploy logistic regression and machine learning to calculate flight risk probability scores across employee populations based on multi-variate signals:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Time since last promotion (> 2.5 years without advancement).</li>\n  <li>Compa-ratio relative to external market surges (&lt; 85% of market rate).</li>\n  <li>Manager change or reorganization within past 6 months.</li>\n  <li>Sudden drop in internal communication platform engagement or PTO spikes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>5. Executive People Dashboard Information Architecture</h2>\n<p>HR Generalists design monthly executive People Dashboards presenting: Headcount Growth vs. Budget, Annualized Attrition Rate, eNPS trendline, Diversity Representation across leadership tiers, and Average Time-to-Fill.</p>"
